b0729d5d252cae05.description:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The Medical Affairs Project Associate Specialist (post-grad trainee) will join the International Medical TTR team and report to International Medical Strategy &amp;amp; Operations. The post-grad trainee will support the planning, governance and execution of the international Medical Affairs Strategy for ATTR-CM across Alnylam&#39;s international markets, working closely with regional and country Medical teams and cross-functional partners. The role contributes to medical operations and planning deliverables, evidence generation portfolio, scientific engagement and insight programs, field medical excellence initiatives and patient experience work and offers first-hand insight into how a regional Medical Affairs organization is run. The scope is intentionally flexible: the more capability, initiative and curiosity the post-grad trainee brings, the more the remit can expand, in line with results.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the International Medical Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team in planning, tracking and reporting on International Medical TTR strategic priorities and operating-model deliverables across international markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help with the preparation of management materials, such as leadership updates, pre-reads, meeting materials and executive presentations, turning complex information into clear, decision-ready outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support medical planning and budget cycles by consolidating regional and country inputs, tracking spend against plan and preparing summaries, in partnership with Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to evidence generation portfolio management by maintaining study trackers (e.g., investigator-initiated studies, research collaborations) and partnering with in preparing status, milestone and timeline overviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support scientific engagement and medical education activities, including the speaker engagement process and congress planning, all scientific and non-promotional in nature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the TOP 41 Centers of Excellence (CoE) program, supporting the project owner in engagement mapping; this is a potential area where the post-grad trainee may take ownership of project deliverables, depending on experience and interest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support field medical excellence initiatives, such as field medical KPIs and dashboards, the quarterly medical insights process, training roll-out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to patient experience work, including patient advocacy and engagement and patient support programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain first-hand insight into the regional medical leadership agenda by supporting cross-functional planning, governance meetings and operational follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Depending on experience and interest, support projects on AI-enabled tools, CRM and insights platforms, and other emerging medical priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability for a minimum of 9 months; 12 months is strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completed bachelor&#39;s degree; a master&#39;s degree is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Academic background in life sciences, medicine, pharmacy, biomedical sciences, public health or another analytical discipline is preferred; interest in Medical Affairs, cardiology or rare diseases is valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong logical and analytical thinking, with the ability to navigate complexity and structure ambiguous problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read, interpret and critically summarize scientific and clinical literature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of, or willingness to learn, the compliance principles that govern Medical Affairs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance PowerPoint and Excel skills; confidence using Microsoft Copilot and AI-enabled productivity tools is highly valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast learner, proactive and adaptive, taking ownership of high-quality outputs and handling confidential information with discretion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills in English; additional languages are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to work 2-3 days per week in the Zug office; occasional travel possible (mainly EU)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, flexible and comfortable working in a fast-moving, cross-functional and international environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to join a highly motivated, science-driven team in a leading RNAi therapeutics company&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on exposure to how International Medical Affairs supports the AMVUTTRA ATTR-CM launch, with a focus on science, evidence and patients&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to contribute to Alnylam&#39;s mission of bringing groundbreaking medicines to patients&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct one-to-one mentoring, supportive supervision, and regular development feedback&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration with a diverse team of experts across medicine, scientific engagement, evidence generation, patient experience, and analytics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong office community, with events and opportunities to connect with colleagues across functions and disciplines&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Alnylam: &lt;/strong&gt;Alnylam Pharmaceuticals (Nasdaq: ALNY) has led the translation of RNA interference (RNAi) into a whole new class of innovative medicines with the potential to transform the lives of people afflicted with rare and more prevalent diseases. Based on Nobel Prize-winning science, RNAi therapeutics represent a powerful, clinically validated approach to treating diseases at their genetic source by “interfering” with mRNA that cause or contribute to disease. Since our founding in 2002, Alnylam has led the RNAi Revolution and continues to turn scientific possibility into reality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our culture:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Our people-first culture is guided by our core values: fiercely innovative, open culture, purposeful urgency, passion for excellence, and commitment to people, and these values influence how we work and the business decisions we make. Thanks to feedback from our employees over the years, we’ve been fortunate to be named a top employer around the world. Alnylam is extremely proud to have been recognized as one of Science Magazine’s Top Biopharma Employers, one of America&#39;s Most Responsible Companies for 2024 by Newsweek, a Fast Company Best Workplace for Innovators, and a Great Place to Work in Canada, France, Italy, Spain, Switzerland, and UK – among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alnylam, we commit to an inclusive recruitment process and equal employment opportunity. We are dedicated to building an environment where employees can feel that they belong, can bring their authentic selves to work, and achieve to their full potential. By empowering employees to embrace their unique differences at work, our business grows stronger with advanced and original thinking, allowing us to bring groundbreaking medicines to patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before applying, please review Alnylam&#39;s ⁠Candidate&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://alnylampolicies.com/&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;regarding how Alnylam handles Personal Data you provide with your application for employment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-CC1&amp;nbsp;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

078b110b319772ff.description:
&lt;p&gt;Auterion builds a cutting-edge operating system for autonomous robotic systems that empower a diverse range of platforms to perform surveillance, reconnaissance, inspection, mapping and logistics tasks. Our industry-leading software drives the adoption of robotic fleets and is recognized by the U.S. government as the future standard for its drone programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Embedded Linux Software Engineer taking on tasks within the AuterionOS ecosystem, from writing applications to adding driver support for new peripherals, maintaining system services and optimizing performance on embedded platforms. You will be working closely with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux running on embedded hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;C/C++, Python &amp;amp; Bash codebases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engaged and friendly engineers from across Auterion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within the Board Support team and collaborate with other development teams to build leading-edge products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add features, solve bugs, write tests and improve the performance of software components running on AuterionOS, Auterion’s custom embedded Linux distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering and product teams to understand both internal and customer use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose new software solutions and take ownership of the implementation. Your technical expertise will have a huge impact on bringing Auterion’s drone products to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide expert support (L3) to customers facing technical issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear and concise internal documentation, in addition to contributing to the public-facing knowledge base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in daily stand-ups, as well as release planning and task prioritization meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.Sc./M.Sc. in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience writing object-oriented C++ and/or Python code in a professional setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience working with embedded architectures, including cross-compilation, debugging, and performance optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert Linux skills, with an excellent grasp of command line operations, resource management, systems services and networking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the Linux kernel, embedded device drivers, device tree configuration and u-boot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Debian/Ubuntu-based systems, Debian packaging workflows and managing complex Docker environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of OTA updates (e.g. mender).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in networking concepts across all layers of the OSI model, including connectors, and hardware interfaces, IP addressing, routing protocols, DNS, HTTP/HTTPS, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in using network diagnostic tools (e.g., Wireshark, tcpdump) to identify and resolve network issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic embedded security knowledge, such as secure boot on embedded devices and/or UEFI, boot chain verification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience with network security protocols (e.g., SSL/TLS, VPNs) and best practices for securing embedded devices, such as secure boot and encryption mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic electrical engineering experience, such as familiarity with schematics and the instrumentation required to debug communication over I2C, SPI, UART, CAN bus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: Experience with video streaming and MIPI CSI drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: Experience with NVIDIA Jetson platforms and their associated BSP packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: Experience with NXP iMX8 platforms and their associated BSP packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: Previous contributions to open source projects, especially in the Linux ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: Experience with CI/CD systems, such as Jenkins, GitHub actions, GitLab CI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in an agile environment, providing daily updates in stand-ups and managing tasks in a sprint board.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product-oriented mindset, with an eagerness to drive forward project initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU Citizenship required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

6c75995ddf7251a6.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Cato Networks is the converged network and security cloud for the AI era.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;As AI reshapes cybersecurity, enterprises face a dual challenge: unlocking AI’s potential while defending against AI-driven attacks. Cato addresses both through a unified, cloud-native platform, providing the visibility and context to prioritize risks and stop threats in real time across users, applications, data, and AI agents.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Join us as we scale: take on ambitious technological challenges and shape the next generation of enterprise security at a company trusted by thousands of organizations worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Major Sales Director who shares our enthusiasm for AI, Cybersecurity and SaaS innovation. If you&#39;re ready to take on the challenge of selling cutting-edge solutions to organizations within a defined territory, we’d love to have you on our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please be aware &lt;/strong&gt;that this is an Individual Contributor position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Sales in Your Territory: &lt;/strong&gt;Own the sales cycle within your assigned region, from prospecting to closing, securing deals with mid-to-large accounts and building lasting relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage with Decision-Makers: &lt;/strong&gt;Connect with key decision-makers (CIOs, CISOs, CTOs) and align our cybersecurity and SaaS solutions with their business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Focus: &lt;/strong&gt;Position our solutions as integral to customers&#39; long-term success and become a trusted advisor within your territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage Sales Cycles: &lt;/strong&gt;Navigate sales cycles of varying lengths, managing multiple stakeholders and maintaining momentum throughout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leverage Data: &lt;/strong&gt;Use sales intelligence, win-loss analysis, and pipeline metrics to refine strategies for ongoing success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate &amp;amp; Share Knowledge: &lt;/strong&gt;Work alongside the sales team, sharing insights and best practices to drive success within the territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner for Growth: &lt;/strong&gt;Develop relationships with local MSSPs, VARs, and other strategic partners to expand market reach and bring solutions to more organisations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay Informed: &lt;/strong&gt;Stay ahead of industry trends and help position our solutions as leaders in the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: 5+ years of experience in territory sales within cybersecurity, SaaS, or related industries, with proven success in managing sales cycles and engaging with decision-makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Success&lt;/strong&gt;: A demonstrated history of consistently meeting or exceeding sales quotas and driving revenue growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;: Strong understanding of cybersecurity, SaaS, or networking solutions, with awareness of current market trends and competitive positioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship-Driven&lt;/strong&gt;: Ability to build long-term, trust-based relationships with key stakeholders and decision-makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative&lt;/strong&gt;: Experience working with partners, MSSPs, VARs, and other strategic collaborators to drive sales and expand business opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LIKD-1&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

ed3bb1e7da231f1f.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join Vinted&#39;s Trust &amp;amp; Safety domain, whose mission is to protect the Vinted community from harmful activities and content. Across several detection, moderation and sanctioning teams, we run a growing set of machine learning models, rule engines, and LLM agents. They score every new listing, account and message at Vinted&#39;s scale, and many of them act on members automatically.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Staff Data Scientist to shape the architecture and effectiveness of our detection systems as a whole. You&#39;ll tackle problems that individual teams cannot solve independently: how to maximize detection coverage, combine different models into coherent risk decisions, and allocate computational resources where they reduce the most harm.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role with scope across Trust &amp;amp; Safety and Security domains. You&#39;ll set technical direction, challenge existing approaches, prototype solutions and work with teams to bring them into production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&#39;s an opportunity to shape how a large-scale, increasingly AI-driven safety system is built, evaluated and improved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the end-to-end ML architecture for detection, risk scoring, routing and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop cost-efficient, layered inference strategies that combine broad, low-latency screening with deeper, more expensive analysis where it adds the most value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish approaches to continuous risk assessment across the member lifecycle, from registration and listing creation to ongoing activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how we measure end-to-end detection effectiveness, including precision, coverage, missed harm and computational cost. Use these measurements to identify the highest-impact improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn siloed, team-level models into a coherent, calibrated detection system by addressing the technical and organisational barriers that lead to local optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and close detection coverage gaps, ensuring that relevant signals and outcomes are available for evaluation, diagnosis and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set shared technical standards and architectural direction across teams, working with engineering and data science leaders to translate them into production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype critical components, test architectural assumptions empirically and build reference implementations that teams can scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain complex ML trade-offs to senior technical and business leaders as clear choices about harm reduction, cost, and engineering investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 8+ years of experience in Data Science, Machine Learning, or a similar role, including significant time owning production models or model evaluation at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have led cross-team technical work without formal authority, and you&#39;re comfortable setting standards that other teams adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have deep expertise in statistical inference and experimentation: A/B testing, measuring precision and recall under imperfect or biased labels, sampling for ground truth, and causal reasoning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the ML lifecycle in production: evaluation, threshold setting, retraining, drift, feature stores and monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on experience evaluating LLM-based systems, or a strong interest in building rigorous methods for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are highly proficient in SQL and Python and comfortable working in a modern data stack (e.g. BigQuery, dbt).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can turn messy, cross-system problems into a clear plan, and can explain trade-offs to both technical and non-technical audiences, including senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are fluent in English, both written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: experience in Trust &amp;amp; Safety, fraud prevention, content moderation, or risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work perks&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to benefit from our share options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days of paid annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Newest MacBook models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent team-building events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office support: we provide IT workstation equipment and a personal budget of up to €540 for home workplace furniture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lunch benefit per working day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A personal monthly budget for shopping on Vinted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collective Defined Contribution Pension plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NS Business Card for your commute to the office by public transport&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company bike leasing scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly budget for a flexible benefits platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from Home allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dog-friendly office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workation policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Better balance holidays with workdays by working remotely! Up to 90 days per year in the EU, of these, 21 days can be spent globally. For non-EU citizens, it&#39;s 21 days worldwide. This can be combined with time off for vacation or personal time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each year, you’ll be given a learning budget (starting at €3,000), and a total of up to 10 working days over a 2-year period to support your personal and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our hybrid model, with 2 recommended office days a week, gives you and your team the flexibility to decide if and when you want to work from home, and when to catch up in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from everybody, regardless of your background, identity, or life experiences. Job openings come with guides, not checklists. If you’re excited about a role, but don’t identify with every point in the ‘About you’ section, apply anyway – you might still be the perfect match!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual gross salary range for this position excluding 8% holiday pay is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€107.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€144.800 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

f39f280a1b9d2f62.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Site Reliability Engineer II on the Kafka team, you&#39;ll build and operate the software and infrastructure behind one of Vinted&#39;s busiest platforms. The Kafka platform spans multiple data centers and regions across the EU and US, 1000+ Kafka brokers across multiple clusters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll develop Kafka as a managed service, automation and client libraries, primarily using Go, Ruby and Java. You&#39;ll take ownership of solutions throughout their lifecycle: from technical design and implementation to deployment and production operation, and help shape the team&#39;s technical direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role balances systems design, backend development, infrastructure setup maintenance, and operations. It suits an experienced, hands-on engineer who wants to work on large-scale infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop managed services and automation for the Kafka platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operate reliable, scalable services on both bare metal and Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical initiatives from design to production, solving complex software and infrastructure problems along the way.&lt;/li&gt;
